  <conditions attached="1">
   <condition type="1">
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Consistent with the Article III of the SBAA [or the Supplemental Provisions to the Project Document], the responsibility for the safety and security of the Implementing Partner and its personnel and property, and of UNDP&#x2019;s property in the Implementing Partner&#x2019;s custody, rests with the Implementing Partner.  To this end, the Implementing Partner shall: a)	put in place an appropriate security plan and maintain the security plan, taking into account the security situation in the country where the project is being carried; b)	assume all risks and liabilities related to the Implementing Partner&#x2019;s security, and the full implementation of the security plan.</narrative>
   </condition>
   <condition type="1">
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Social and environmental sustainability will be enhanced through application of the UNDP Social and Environmental Standards (http://www.undp.org/ses) and related Accountability Mechanism (http://www.undp.org/secu-srm).</narrative>
   </condition>
  </conditions>
  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.Existence of revised Environmental Policy 
2.Number of sectors with Green Technologies need assessed conducted and implemented
3.No of sectors developed CRGE strategies and action plans  in gender sensitive manner
4.Preparation of principles and standards to be accredited by the GCF;
5.Amount of funds available in the CRGE Facility
6.Number of Capacity Building Program document for the CRGE strategy  implementation  developed
7. Number of national, regional and woreda institutions having the necessary human resource, technical capacity, system and procedures to plan, coordinate and implement resilience building activities in particular and sustainable natural resource malmanagement in general
8.Number of bankable projects developed;
9.No of global CC negotiation attended by key sectors
10.Existence Private sector engagement frame work  for RGE implementation</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2012">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.	There are no revised Environmental Policy, 
2.	The assessment of needs for Green Technologies has not adequately covered all sectors and regions 
3.	sector specific CRGE strategies, action plans, and implementation tools etc  not yet completed.
4.	CRGE facility not accredited by GCF;
5.	CRGE Facility is unable to raise adequate funds
6.	Capacity Building Program for the CRGE implementation   not developed;
7.	Inadequate resilience building activities and  poor conservation and unsustainable management of natural capital
8.	Lack of skill for formulating bankable projects and preparing investment proposals
9.	Global Climate Change negotiation capacity enhanced
10.	Absence Private sector engagement frame work in CRGE implementation</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.CRGE facility tools and systems rolled understanding created at regional and local levels;
2. Climate finance contributors to the CRGE Facility increased by 20% from the current level:
3. Ministry Of finance accreditation to GCF increased</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.CRGE facility tools and systems rolled understanding created at regional and local levels through awareness raising by the MoF
2. With the support of UNDP Ministry of Finance accreditation increased to 200 million USD
3. MoF accreditation to GCF substantially increased.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Three more locally available available technologies selected 
Two country reports on global climate change negotiation prepared and submitted 
Two fact sheets on two critical ecosystems produced
two mega projects monitored and inspected and reports produced
climate finance tracking for the water, irrigation and energy sectors study conducted
 Support the MOF GCF accreditation status upgrading 
Finalize the Climate Smart Development plans preparation
Organize training and workshops on climate change, project cycle management, and climate finance for federal, regional and local stakeholders
Awareness raising workshop on waste management for 200 participants given during the World Environment Day
Document on valuation of forest and wetland ecosystems produced</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Three more locally available technologies selected and two facts sheets on two critical ecosystem produced; Two country reports on climate change negotiation drafted. Climate finance tracking for the water, irrigation and energy sectors conducted. Technical support provided for upgrading the accreditation level of MoF to GCF. Draft Climate Smart Development Plan for seven districts selected from Oromia; SNNP; Diredawa City Administration; Harari National Regional State; Tigray National Regional State and Amhara National Regional States prepared. The Plans being finalized by 2021. Two mega projects monitored .inspected and reports produced</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. 12 environmental School clubs will be supported 
2. 100 persons will be sensitized on harmfulness of waste pollution for the larger public.
3. One Training workshop organized for Experts drawn from IPs at federal and regional levels on investment proposal preparation for CRGE supported projects</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
    </period>
   </indicator>
